   "4": [
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "4.1 Description of first aid measures."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "In case of doubt or when symptoms of feeling unwell persist, get medical attention. Never administer anything orally to persons who are unconscious."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Inhalation. Take the victim into open air; keep them warm and calm. If breathing is irregular or stops, perform artificial respiration. Do not administer anything orally. If unconscious, place them in a suitable position and seek medical assistance."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Eye contact. Remove contact lenses, if present and if it is easy to do. Wash eyes with plenty of clean and cool water for at least 10 minutes while pulling eyelids up, and seek medical assistance."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Skin contact. Remove contaminated clothing. Wash skin vigorously with water and soap or a suitable skin cleaner. NEVER use solvents or thinners."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Ingestion. If accidentally ingested, seek immediate medical attention. Keep calm. NEVER induce vomiting."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "4.2 Most important symptoms and effects, both acute and delayed."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Corrosive Product, contact with eyes or skin can cause burns; ingestion or inhalation can cause internal damage, if this occurs immediate medical assistance is required."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "4.3 Indication of any immediate medical attention and special treatment needed."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "In case of doubt or when symptoms of feeling unwell persist, get medical attention. Never administer anything orally to persons who are unconscious. Cover the affected area with a dry sterile bandage. Protect the affected area from pressure or friction."
    }
   ],
   "6": [
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "6.1 Personal precautions, protective equipment and emergency procedures."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "For exposure control and individual protection measures, see section 8."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "6.2 Environmental precautions."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Product not classified as hazardous for the environment, avoid spillage as much as possible."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "6.3 Methods and material for containment and cleaning up."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Contain and collect spillage with inert absorbent material (earth, sand, vermiculite, Kieselguhr...) and clean the area immediately with a suitable decontaminant. Deposit waste in closed and suitable containers for disposal, in compliance with local and national regulations (see section 13)."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "6.4 Reference to other sections."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "For exposure control and individual protection measures, see section 8. For later elimination of waste, follow the recommendations under section 13."
    }
   ],
   "5": [
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "The product is NOT classified as flammable, in case of fire the following measures should be taken:"
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "5.1 Extinguishing media."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Suitable extinguishing media: Extinguisher powder or CO2. In case of more serious fires, also alcohol-resistant foam and water spray."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Unsuitable extinguishing media: Do not use a direct stream of water to extinguish. In the presence of electrical voltage, you cannot use water or foam as extinguishing media."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "5.2 Special hazards arising from the substance or mixture."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Special risks. Exposure to combustion or decomposition products can be harmful to your health."
    },
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "5.3 Advice for firefighters."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Use water to cool tanks, cisterns, or containers close to the heat source or fire. Take wind direction into account. Prevent the products used to fight the fire from going into drains, sewers, or waterways."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Fire protection equipment. According to the size of the fire, it may be necessary to use protective suits against the heat, individual breathing equipment, gloves, protective goggles or facemasks, and boots."
    }
   ],
   "13": [
    {
     "soort": "kop",
     "tekst": "13.1 Waste treatment methods."
    },
    {
     "soort": "alinea",
     "tekst": "Do not dump into sewers or waterways. Waste and empty containers must be handled and eliminated according to current, local/national legislation. Follow the provisions of Directive 2008/98/EC regarding waste management."
    }
   ]
